{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_{syntomic}/S$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0009": "$(\\Sch/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0010": "$U/S$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\Sch/S)_{syntomic}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-localize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-small-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:17505fea6489aa89a46ef9d9b971aaf5a9a419b83d2a220694c604604b2c3f62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9bb07944ea9e32a4049bac5c3c54a70d3cbe91a3bcaacedfbc0d134ef1eae247", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big syntomic\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big syntomic site of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, denoted\n<MATH_0005>, is the site <MATH_0006>\nintroduced in Sites, Section <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The <TEXTITOPEN_0002>big affine syntomic site of <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, denoted\n<MATH_0008>, is the full subcategory of\n<MATH_0009> whose objects are affine <MATH_0010>.\nA covering of <MATH_0011> is any covering\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> which is a\nstandard syntomic covering.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a01a906e037cf18f297b0e68b75b8822c36c06b6403bc7710d9a02f988fa63a1", "unit_id": "tag:03X3:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f66aaba62f27af3d693f62e01cfa6b5803f9ba6e4af5451d7ac6a760574e643", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we check that the big affine site defines the same\ntopos as the big site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78c6b1773b894b6b6a83aad54cff4dcbe080120f2b8498c883a3a9768e16ad14", "unit_id": "tag:0224:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{syntomic} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh((\\textit{Aff}/S)_{syntomic})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_{syntomic})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-big-site-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c60496b7d852a0b85012fffe12fa0508dc640b707fa8c217520dded8f84b0089", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db37877fde0b3e3e8602e4eef99f35e1ae9bb4af3b7b632d38790dec0af5bc3e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big syntomic\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0004>\nis special cocontinuous and induces an equivalence of topoi from\n<MATH_0005> to\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:28da77e88dc1e241fde9101c9c34b338085bbf55c3b696093346b8657769f422", "unit_id": "tag:06VD:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0224", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : (\\textit{Aff}/S)_{syntomic} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{syntomic}$", "MATH_0002": "$T/S$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-special-cocontinuous-functor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-equivalence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-syntomic-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e146f427711d905e26b21b00106e7b633727697dad5cc5be4f5e1354f0d731a5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f9a3736cfd8b12b35692eab0587693a32db790619673af13b6431b3beed2dea3", "source_text": "The notion of a special cocontinuous functor is introduced in\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nThus we have to verify assumptions (1) -- (5) of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nDenote the inclusion functor\n<MATH_0001>.\nBeing cocontinuous just means that any syntomic covering of\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> affine, can be refined by a standard syntomic covering of <MATH_0004>.\nThis is the content of\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nHence (1) holds. We see <MATH_0005> is continuous simply because a standard\nsyntomic covering is a syntomic covering. Hence (2) holds.\nParts (3) and (4) follow immediately from the fact that <MATH_0006> is\nfully faithful. And finally condition (5) follows from the\nfact that every scheme has an affine open covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c0ee06625b9d477a88462bbf66adc6347396609d2b3367e07b2897f11184f4e4", "unit_id": "tag:06VD:proof"}
